<title>INDONESIA: Jababeka Q1 net up sharply at 67 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Jababeka Q1 net up sharply at 67 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian property developer PT Kawasan Industri Jababeka said on Friday it posted net profit of 67 billion rupiah in the 1997 first quarter against 23 billion rupiah in the same 1996 period.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the sharp rise was boosted by the sale of 170 hectares of undeveloped land.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale of the raw land contributed 95 billion rupiah to the total sales of 194 billion rupiah,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>It said total sales in the first quarter of 1996 were 78 billion rupiah.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
